# The vectors a reader fails when this rule is deleted, and no others:
# a ranged int decodes to its offset plus min.
#
# CMakeLists.txt builds that reader, and ctest requires its failures to be
# exactly this list. A vector added to the corpus that pins the rule belongs here.

int-negative-min-golden-field
int-negative-min-accepts-its-minimum
int-negative-min-accepts-its-maximum
int-full-int32-range-golden-field
int-full-int32-range-minimum
int-full-int32-range-maximum
bounded-3-accept-low
bounded-3-accept-high
bounded-3-accept-at-domain-top
bounded-5-accept-low
bounded-5-accept-high
bounded-5-accept-at-domain-top
bounded-9-accept-low
bounded-9-accept-high
bounded-9-accept-at-domain-top
bounded-13-accept-low
